## Real-browser verification

Same technique as VTID-03822 (no live gateway/Supabase credentials in this
session): served the real, unmodified `services/gateway/src/frontend/
command-hub/` tree at `/command-hub/*` via a local static file server, and
drove the real code in headless Chromium (Playwright, /opt/pw-browsers/
chromium).

### Filter chips + staleness badge + bulk-select (desktop + mobile)

Seeded 5 fake tasks via `state.tasks` (one Scheduled task deliberately
12 days old, `is_terminal` unset — the "stale" case) and mounted the real
`renderTasksView()` output outside `#root` (so the app's own auth-gate
re-render loop can't clobber the harness). Screenshotted at 1400x900 and
390x844:
  - /tmp/vtid03823-board-desktop.png
  - /tmp/vtid03823-board-mobile.png
  - /tmp/vtid03823-board-stale-filter.png (after clicking the real
    "Stale (>7d)" chip)
All three sent to the user directly.

Clicked the real "Stale (>7d)" chip: querying
`.task-card-vtid-label` afterward showed exactly `["VTID-10002"]` visible
— the one seeded stale task, across all three columns.

Clicked a real checkbox via `page.click()`: `state.taskMultiSelectIds`
updated and the bulk-action bar rendered with the correct count (visible
in the mobile screenshot).

### Drag-and-drop (Scheduled -> In Progress)

Seeded two Scheduled tasks, one `spec_status: 'approved'` one `'draft'`.
Stubbed `window.fetch` to intercept and record any
`PATCH /api/v1/oasis/tasks/:vtid` call instead of hitting a live backend,
then used Playwright's real `locator.dragTo()` (genuine HTML5 drag-and-
drop, not a synthetic click) to drag each card onto the real "In
Progress" column's drop zone:

  - Dragging the DRAFT (unapproved) task -> 0 PATCH calls recorded (gate
    held, no toast-triggering network call).
  - Dragging the APPROVED task -> the real `confirm()` dialog fired with
    the exact text "Move VTID-20001 to In Progress for manual work? ...
    This will NOT trigger autonomous execution — you will work on this
    task yourself." Accepting it produced exactly one recorded call:
    `{"url":"/api/v1/oasis/tasks/VTID-20001","body":"{\"status\":\"in_progress\"}"}`.

### Pre-existing zero-height status-row bug (found while verifying the age badge)

Directly measured `getBoundingClientRect()` on `.task-card-status-row`
and its children for a real card rendered by the real `createTaskCard()`:

  - Against `origin/main` (checked out via `git show origin/main:...` into
    a separate static root, BEFORE this VTID's own CSS changes): row
    height measured 0px; status pill/role badge each individually had
    nonzero size but were clipped to invisible by the 0-height,
    `overflow:hidden` parent.
  - After removing `overflow:hidden` + adding `flex-shrink:0` on the row
    alone: row height became 18px and all three badges (status/age/role)
    became visible — but `.task-card-spec-row`/`.task-stage-timeline`
    (which come after the status row in the same flex-column card, capped
    at `max-height:100px`) now clipped instead, confirmed by the same
    rect measurement and by screenshot.
  - After additionally raising `.task-card-enhanced`'s `max-height` from
    100px to 148px (the measured natural sum of title + vtid-line +
    3-item status row + spec-row + stage-timeline): every row's rect
    matched its natural content height, nothing clipped. Re-screenshotted
    the full board to confirm — all badges, spec pills, and PL/WO/VA/DE
    stage pills visible simultaneously on every card
    (/tmp/vtid03823-board-desktop.png, sent to the user).

Cleaned up: removed all ad-hoc Playwright driver scripts (not part of the
shipped diff) and the temporary static file servers/roots.

